# state: returning   (rallisport-2.returning's menus; a new drive loop after the mark)
# RalliSport Challenge 2 (4D530039): Time Attack, Crossover, Australia / Copperhead, Hyundai Accent Evo 3.
# lane.ralli2audio1018, 2026-10-18, #433: the audio starve in the owner's 10-18 capture came while racing.
# Copied unchanged below this header by lane.fpsdata1018 (texscan 2D A/B, #433); its race measured 41-44 gfps
# on the Nova in four ralli2audio1018 runs, against 18-27 in the owner's race.
#
# Why a new loop: rallisport-2.returning's loop opens with 2.5 s of full LT. At the mark the car stands on
# the start line facing the straight (10-12 run 1-1791822916-lane.local-3120610, shot `gameplay`: 0 mph,
# race clock 00:23), so the reverse backs it off the grid into the paddock behind the start, where it sat
# for the rest of the run (frames at race clock 01:12 and 02:15: car against the paddock fence, minimap
# marker behind the start line). That run measured a stationary car: audio short 0.0, which says nothing
# about racing.
#
# This loop holds RT from the mark and weaves the stick in short pulses, so the barriers on both sides
# keep the car in the channel, and every ~14 s it brakes and reverses on right lock for 1.5 s, which frees
# a car pinned against a barrier and only slows a moving one. Blind; the soak's periodic frames (race
# clock, LAP, minimap marker) say how far it got.
